WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:14.355
Hook swam toward the pirate boat in the growing darkness.

2
00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:17.497
Starkey held out the lantern to guide him.

3
00:00:18.597 --> 00:00:23.460
Meanwhile, Wendy and Peter were still in the water listening closely to what was happening.

4
00:00:24.621 --> 00:00:26.802
Hook reached the boat and climbed on board.

5
00:00:26.822 --> 00:00:30.404
"Captain, is everything okay?"

6
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.421
Smee asked timidly.

7
00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.482
All Hook could do was let out a sigh.

8
00:00:39.784 --> 00:00:40.424
up, Captain?"

9
00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:42.165
Smee asked again.

10
00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:44.826
Finally the captain spoke.

11
00:00:44.846 --> 00:00:46.346
"The game is over.

12
00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:49.988
Those boys have found a mother to help them."

13
00:00:52.209 --> 00:00:53.109
He sighed again.

14
00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.370
Wendy felt very proud.

15
00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.752
"Oh, what an evil day!"

16
00:01:00.436 --> 00:01:01.277
cried Starkey.

17
00:01:01.297 --> 00:01:03.259
"How dreadful!

18
00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:05.220
But what's a mother?"

19
00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:06.581
asked Smee.

20
00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:10.765
Wendy was so shocked that she gave out a little yell.

21
00:01:11.786 --> 00:01:14.608
Peter had to pull her under the water to keep her quiet.

22
00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:18.772
Hook heard the noise and said, "What's that?"

23
00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:24.657
"Nothing but the birds," answered Starkey, raising the lantern.

24
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:28.520
They could see a nest floating on the lagoon.

25
00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:31.557
A big bird sat on top of it.

26
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:36.440
"See?" said Hook to Smee, pointing to the bird.

27
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.521
"That is a mother.

28
00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:41.082
That nest has fallen into the water.

29
00:01:42.343 --> 00:01:44.164
But does the mother desert her eggs?

30
00:01:45.265 --> 00:01:47.906
No! She will sit on them until they hatch.

31
00:01:49.227 --> 00:01:51.208
Then they will become her children.

32
00:01:52.468 --> 00:01:58.752
She protects them from all dangers, like falling into the water or being eaten up by fish."

33
00:02:00.436 --> 00:02:03.397
Hook's description made the pirates wipe tears from their eyes.

34
00:02:04.478 --> 00:02:09.340
As they watched the mother bird protecting her young, Smee suddenly had an idea.

35
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:17.803
"Captain," said Smee, "maybe we could kidnap the Lost Boys' new mother and make her our mother instead."

36
00:02:17.823 --> 00:02:20.724
"What a great idea!"

37
00:02:21.464 --> 00:02:22.145
cried Hook.

38
00:02:22.165 --> 00:02:26.326
"We will seize the children and carry them to our ship.

39
00:02:27.687 --> 00:02:31.180
We will make the boys walk the plank.

40
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.321
Then the girl will become our mother!"

41
00:02:34.561 --> 00:02:36.362
"Never!" cried Wendy.

42
00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.443
Peter had to push her under the water again.

43
00:02:39.463 --> 00:02:41.564
"What was that?"

44
00:02:42.325 --> 00:02:44.666
said Hook, trying to listen in the dark.

45
00:02:45.746 --> 00:02:47.127
But everything was quiet now.

46
00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:51.348
Then the captain and his pirates shook hands and hook.

47
00:02:52.309 --> 00:02:53.809
They all swore to the plan.

48
00:02:53.829 --> 00:03:01.132
"Yes, a girl and a mother is just what we need," said Smee, as if he knew all

49
00:03:01.193 --> 00:03:02.193
about mothers now.

50
00:03:03.774 --> 00:03:07.715
Suddenly, Captain Hook remembered another girl—Tiger Lily.

51
00:03:07.735 --> 00:03:10.577
"Where is the Indian princess?"

52
00:03:11.277 --> 00:03:11.917
he demanded.

53
00:03:11.937 --> 00:03:17.460
"We let her go, just like you told us," said Starkey.

54
00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.761
"You let her go?"

55
00:03:20.521 --> 00:03:21.381
screamed Hook.

56
00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.022
"It was your order.

57
00:03:24.623 --> 00:03:27.424
You told us to let her go," said Smee.

58
00:03:28.556 --> 00:03:29.657
"That's ridiculous!

59
00:03:30.017 --> 00:03:31.418
I gave no such order."

60
00:03:32.358 --> 00:03:36.941
Realizing his pirates had been tricked, Hook turned back to the voice he had heard in the dark

61
00:03:36.981 --> 00:03:41.023
lagoon. He yelled out, "Do you hear me?"

62
00:03:42.444 --> 00:03:45.885
Though he knew he shouldn't answer, Peter couldn't stop himself.

63
00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:47.786
"I hear you!"

64
00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:51.308
he called back, imitating Hook's voice once again.

65
00:03:51.328 --> 00:03:53.990
"Who are you, stranger?"

66
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.651
Hook demanded.

67
00:03:56.751 --> 00:04:02.007
Peter yelled back, "I am Captain James Hook of the Jolly Roger."

68
00:04:02.027 --> 00:04:03.928
"You are not!"

69
00:04:04.488 --> 00:04:05.369
exclaimed Hook.

70
00:04:05.389 --> 00:04:07.971
"If you are Hook, who am I?"

71
00:04:07.991 --> 00:04:10.512
"A codfish!"

72
00:04:10.993 --> 00:04:11.793
replied the voice.

73
00:04:11.813 --> 00:04:14.215
"A codfish?"

74
00:04:14.916 --> 00:04:16.397
said Hook, confused.

75
00:04:17.577 --> 00:04:20.319
Smee and Starkey drew back from their captain.

76
00:04:20.339 --> 00:04:23.702
"Our captain is a codfish?

77
00:04:24.322 --> 00:04:26.824
How embarrassing," they said.

78
00:04:28.384 --> 00:04:32.347
Humiliated, Captain Hook decided to challenge the voice.

79
00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:35.050
"Have you got another name?"

80
00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.211
he called.

81
00:04:37.151 --> 00:04:42.296
Peter could never resist a good game, so he answered, "Yes, I have."

82
00:04:42.316 --> 00:04:44.477
"Is it vegetable?"

83
00:04:45.078 --> 00:04:45.698
asked Hook.

84
00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:48.721
"No," Peter answered.

85
00:04:48.741 --> 00:04:51.063
"Mineral?" "No."

86
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:52.864
"Animal?" "Yes."

87
00:04:52.884 --> 00:04:56.107
"A man?"

88
00:04:56.787 --> 00:04:57.348
asked Hook.

89
00:04:58.344 --> 00:04:59.305
"Certainly not!"

90
00:04:59.885 --> 00:05:01.587
cried Peter, annoyed.

91
00:05:01.607 --> 00:05:04.129
"A boy?"

92
00:05:04.149 --> 00:05:05.690
"Yes, yes."

93
00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.932
"An ordinary boy?"

94
00:05:07.952 --> 00:05:15.238
"No! A very special boy," answered Peter, losing himself in the fun of the game.

95
00:05:16.659 --> 00:05:20.922
"Hmm," said Hook, pretending to be puzzled.

96
00:05:20.942 --> 00:05:22.864
"Can't you guess?"

97
00:05:23.484 --> 00:05:24.305
cried Peter.

98
00:05:24.325 --> 00:05:26.347
"Or do you give up?"

99
00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:29.805
"Yes," said Hook eagerly.

100
00:05:29.825 --> 00:05:31.185
"I give up."

101
00:05:32.866 --> 00:05:34.447
"I'm Peter Pan!"

102
00:05:35.007 --> 00:05:36.748
shouted Peter with great pride.

103
00:05:36.768 --> 00:05:39.069
"Now we have him!"

104
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.190
Hook cried gleefully.

105
00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.672
"Into the water, Smee and Starkey.

106
00:05:45.172 --> 00:05:47.013
Take him, dead or alive."

107
00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.455
Hook leapt back into the water.
